  "notes": "JOURNAL 'r' [AT f] [FROM ...] is SELECT date, flag, maxwidth(payee, 48), maxwidth(narration, 80), account, f(position), f(balance) WHERE account ~ \"r\", with no ORDER BY: rows come in ledger order (by date, then source order). The pattern is the case-insensitive partial-match ~ regex. Column names are beanquery's (MAXWIDTH(payee, 48), ...) and advisory only. JOURNAL takes no WHERE, ORDER BY or LIMIT. Every matched account has one posting per day, so the order and the running balance do not depend on ties."
